  "def-nagata-two-open-graph-extensions",
  "def-nagata-two-open-intermediate-schemes"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Let a point of the image specialize to $(u,x)$ in the displayed target. If\n$u\\notin U_i$, then\n[lemma-nagata-intermediate-specialization-boundary] gives\n$x\\in\\overline Z_{i,j}$, contradicting the definition of the target.\nHence $u\\in U_i$. By part (1) of\n[lemma-nagata-key-boundary-disjointness], the identity\n$\\psi_i^{-1}(U_i)=U_i$ forces the point $v$ supplied by\n[lemma-nagata-intermediate-specialization-boundary] to lie in $U_i$.\nThe chosen isomorphism $U_i\\cong\\psi_i^{-1}(U_i)$ then identifies $x$ with\nthe graph point of $u$, so $(u,x)$ is again in the image of $U_i$.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-nagata-intermediate-specialization-boundary",
    "lemma-nagata-key-boundary-disjointness"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
